00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:24.860
I’ll be sure to include new information
if anything about that changes.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:30.461
There are some interesting castings for episodes
8 through the finale but I’ll talk more

00:00:30.461 --> 00:00:31.720
about them when those episodes get here.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:37.110
Heads up too, The Doctor Who Legacy video
game people reached out to me about doing

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:44.900
a special giveaway for episode 7 this saturday,
so be sure to subscribe to get that video.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.610
Question time, careful for spoilers from this
week’s episode in case you haven’t seen

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:48.610
it yet.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.360
I’ll wait just a sec... okay, here we go.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.560
1 - Tasman Devil asks Will there be more Courtney
Woods in the future, do you think she’ll

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.640
die and go to Missy?

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.050
I already answered the first part of that,
I do think your second part is interesting.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:07.000
Moffat is the writer, and he is probably going
for maximum cry levels.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.160
Killing a child feels a little too cruel though,
even for him.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.000
I know there have been times during Classic
Who when children died, but just going on

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.610
Moffat’s own personal history, I think it’s
more likely he’d kill an adult beloved character.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.780
Something about killing innocent children
just makes it feel like something the BBC

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.810
wouldn’t want him to do.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.050
2 - Dragon Fly Noir asks do you agree with
the criticism that Doctor Who this season

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.080
has been too similar to Sherlock?

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.130
I haven’t seen a lot of that sentiment on
the videos I’ve been doing for Doctor Who

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.460
this year so I’ll assume you're talking
about professional critics.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.090
I noticed a lot of Sherlocky-ness in the premiere,
but I think that’s because Vastra’s character

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.210
has always been linked to Sherlock Holmes.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.350
I think any connection to Benedict Cumberbatch’s
Sherlock Series is coincidence.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:56.049
Yes there are Sherlock overtones, but I think
when we’ve seen them, they’ve been endemic

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.280
to the characters.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.880
Now if they played the Sherlock BBC theme
song in the background.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.750
That would probably be too much.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:10.509
3 - Andrew asks, what was the bit with the
Planet in the beginning all about?

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:15.109
The montage was just way to show Clara was
constantly running from adventure to adventure

00:02:15.109 --> 00:02:18.819
with the Doctor in between school.

00:02:18.819 --> 00:02:22.230
I’m not sure what the planet they were on
was, but if anyone thinks they know just write

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.659
it in the comments.

00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:26.450
They also visited fish people and a bunch
of other places.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:30.639
It gives you a sense of the sheer quantity
of stories happening that we never get to

00:02:30.639 --> 00:02:31.639
witness.

00:02:31.639 --> 00:02:36.560
Like we only see the doctor for about 50 minutes
a week which comprises a single adventure.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.810
But outside of that he could being going on
hundreds of other adventures.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:44.140
That’s really where the expanded material
picks things up.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:50.049
4 - Alex Wilcox asks, do you think Danny and
Clara will get married and they’ll use that

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:52.750
as the excuse if Jenna Coleman to leaves the
show?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.989
I think they’re definitely pushing them
in that direction.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:03.390
Most of the romantic companions in recent
years have gotten pseudo happy endings, like

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.159
Amy got Rory, Rose got a version of The Doctor.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:08.980
It might be Moffat setting up a huge twist.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:13.819
I think he’ll make everyone really happy
with the idea that Clara will get married

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:16.529
and have a wonderful life and then yank the
rug out from under us.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:20.090
It just feels like the very TV-thing to do.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:27.529
Make you love a character, then kill them
off.

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:34.449
5 - Chris Paul asks, what do you think the
best episode so far is?

00:03:34.449 --> 00:03:40.079
Right now it’s still Listen, but based on
what the Doctor Who people are saying about

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:43.919
Kill the Moon, that might end up being the
fan favorite.

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:50.370
6 - Drew asks what do you think the policeman
saw through the window at the end?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.669
When you rewatch the scene you can see Chris
Addison from In the Thick of it, smiling.

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:59.040
Like he’s very happy revealing the policeman’s
new environment.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.510
But the policeman is in complete shock.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.129
Not the kind of shock you see on someone’s
face christmas morning opening gifts.

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:11.040
The kind of shock you see on someone’s face
when they’re told they have cancer.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.120
It looks a little bit like Horror.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.949
Something about what he saw fundamentally
changed his core belief system.

00:04:14.949 --> 00:04:15.949
Just to differentiate.

00:04:15.949 --> 00:04:18.840
Terror is the fear you feel when a giant moon
spider is chasing you.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.849
It doesn’t make you question your identity.

00:04:20.849 --> 00:04:23.440
Horror is a profound shock to your belief
system.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.590
Like Oswin Oswald realizing she had been turned
into a Dalek.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:27.590
That’s genuine Horror.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.810
And it looks like that’s what’s going
on here.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.760
7 - a person asks, what’s with all the shared
Moffat Writing Credits on episodes this year?

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.880
I’ve heard a lot of rumors flying around
about drama in the production offices, but

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.020
mostly I think it’s because of the story
structure this year.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.199
They’re making episode less serialized,
but they still have to service the overarching

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:50.300
plots like Missy and Danny Pink with Clara.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.389
Part of Moffat’s role as showrunner is to
make sure they don’t lose sight of those

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:54.389
things.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.370
So he probably jumped on a lot of the scripts
to make sure they tied in with things we’ll

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.710
see happening in the finale.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:06.810
I’m sure he does a lot of other edits to
the stories, but in general.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.650
Adding a writing credit for himself to a script
means he wrote a significant portion of it

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.360
himself.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.560
Those parts being the big stuff going on in
the background.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.431
8 - Why Not asks, I miss the big Epic Moments
that Matt Smith got, do you think we’ll

00:05:21.431 --> 00:05:23.770
get some of those this year?

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:27.919
Part of the reason Matt Smith got those crazy
big moments was because his run was more serialized,

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:32.150
so they had more time to build up to big payoffs.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:36.270
Yes I do think we’ll get some major Capaldi
moments, but I think we won’t start seeing

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.610
those developing till much later in the series.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.460
Episode 7 is supposed to be pretty epic though.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.340
Bloggers are saying it will change the course
of the series.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:52.539
9 - Colin Daley asks do you think Danny Pink
being on the TARDIS this year will cause The

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:55.379
Doctor to go darker and become the valeyard?

00:05:55.379 --> 00:06:05.419
I actually think The Doctor will warm up 
to Danny, maybe not as much as the 11th Doctor

00:06:05.419 --> 00:06:11.069
warmed up to Rory, but as warm as a grumpy
old Scottish Doctor can get.

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:14.409
Trust is a big theme this year, so it makes
sense that The Doctor and Danny would start

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:18.229
to trust each other right as that trust gets
broken.

00:06:18.229 --> 00:06:21.939
As for the valeyard no, I don’t think he’s
going to turn into the Valeyard.

00:06:21.939 --> 00:06:32.479
10 - Mr Nobody asks what does Ozzie loves
the Squaddie mean?

00:06:32.479 --> 00:06:35.440
It’s shorthand for Clara loves Danny.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.000
Ozzie as in Oswald and Squaddie is a reference
to Military Squadron.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.039
Clara and Danny made a remark early in the
episode where Clara asks Danny if the girls

00:06:45.039 --> 00:06:47.569
including Courtney there, know about the two
of them dating.

00:06:47.569 --> 00:06:50.569
Danny said possibly, they’re children, they’ve
got minds of their own.

00:06:50.569 --> 00:06:55.849
I think it just says something about the intelligence
of Children.

00:06:55.849 --> 00:06:58.860
Like children are much more perceptive than
adults.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:04.669
Maybe we’ll see more of that play out with
the Courtney character in episode 7.

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:08.819
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions
though.

